"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin the device rows of a text `<input>` value at device scale k > 1,
against Chrome 159.

Chrome lays the value out on the control font's `normal` line at the DEVICE
size and centres that line in the DEVICE content box, the half px rounding
down the page; the text hangs from the device strut baseline. Simple centred
the line in CSS px (then x k) and hung the text from the painter's ascent at
the rounded device size, with no device correction:
- 13.333px DejaVu Sans Mono at k=4: device line 63, baseline 50, painter
  ascent 49 -> the value sat one device row high (330 vs Chrome 331). The same
  for a 16px Liberation Sans input (614 vs 615).
- `height:40px` at k=4: CSS centring gives 4 x 13 = 52, device centring
  (160 - 61 + 1) / 2 = 50 -> two rows low (383 vs 381).
- k=3, 13.333px Liberation Sans: device strut baseline 35 against the
  painter's 36 -> one row low.
The catalog forms-media `Name` input (13.333px Liberation Sans, auto height)
already matched at k=4: there both terms are 48.

Only the UA control font (13.333px) is moved. The page also holds a 16px and
a 20px monospace input; their boxes are not Chrome's height yet (16px
Liberation Sans: 19 CSS px here, 18 in Chrome), so the rule is not applied to
them. AC-8 guards that: the 16px value stays on rows 460..492 at k=3 and
307..328 at k=2, where it already was and where Chrome has it (the rule on
Simple's 19 px line would give 461 and 308).
At k=3 Simple's 40 px DejaVu Sans Mono `E` is one row taller at the top than
Chrome's (rasterizer); that cell is pinned by its last row, the baseline.

Audience: web renderer form-control paint (paint_draw_ir input value command)
and layout_foundation device line metric maintainers.

Chrome oracle (Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6 aarch64, `--headless=new
--disable-gpu --hide-scrollbars --force-device-scale-factor=k
--window-size=400,300 --screenshot`). Rows holding a pixel with red < 128,
device px. ABS page, left column (x 12..80 CSS): catalog-styled input,
monospace, 16px, default UA input (its inset top border, then the value);
right column (x 200..270): no padding/border, height:40px, height:41px, 20px
monospace.
- k=4 left 87..123 331..369 615..658 880..887 903..939; right 51..87 381..417
  663..699 896..953.
- k=3 left 64..91 247..275 460..492 660..665 676..703; right 37..64 285..312
  496..523 671..714.
- k=2 left 44..61 164..183 307..328 440..443 452..469; right 26..43 191..208
  332..349 447..475.
- k=1 left 22..30 82..91 152..163 220..221 226..234; right 13..21 96..104
  166..174 225..238.
FLOW page (inputs on `<label>` lines, the catalog's control style; label text
white so only the values ink), x 40..200 CSS, first two lines (catalog
style, monospace): k=4 79..115 244..282.
CTL page (the same command also paints button-type values, placeholders and
fallback-font values). Left column: UA submit (value rows inside its border,
x 18..44, y 14..27 CSS), `type=button` and `type=reset` + height:40px with no
border/padding, a placeholder (#757575, read by its last row: the baseline);
right column: an Arabic value (DejaVu Sans fallback), a placeholder in a 40px
field, a monospace UA submit (x 208..232, y 224..237).
- k=4: submit 63..99, button 331..367, reset 661..697, placeholder last row
  927, 40px placeholder last row 697, monospace submit 903..941.
- k=3: submit 46..73, button 247..274, reset 495..522, placeholder last row
  694, 40px placeholder last row 522, monospace submit last row 704, Arabic
  value 246..284 (247..284 when the fallback face's own device offset was
  dropped by a second `device-y-offset` prop).
The Arabic value at k=2 / k=4 and a CJK value are not on Chrome's rows for
other reasons (glyph extents; open) and are not pinned.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-WEB-INPUT-DEVICE-LINE-001 — at device scale k a text input's value sits on Chrome's device `normal` line, centred in the device content box.
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, paint, form_control, device_scale, chrome159
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_paint_draw_ir.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_layout_engine2d_fast.{
    simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale
}

val CSS_W: i32 = 400
val CSS_H: i32 = 300
val ABS: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:#fff;color:#000}}input{{position:absolute;color:#000;background:#fff}}</style></head><body><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:10px;padding:8px;border:1px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:5px\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:10px;padding:0;border:0\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:80px;padding:0;border:0;font-family:monospace\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:80px;padding:0;border:0;height:40px\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:150px;padding:0;border:0;font-size:16px\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:150px;padding:0;border:0;height:41px\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:220px\"><input value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:220px;padding:0;border:0;font-size:20px;font-family:monospace\"></body></html>"
val CTL: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:#fff;color:#000}}input{{position:absolute;color:#000;background:#fff}}</style></head><body><input type=\"submit\" value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:10px\"><input type=\"button\" value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:80px;border:0;padding:0\"><input type=\"reset\" value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:150px;border:0;padding:0;height:40px\"><input placeholder=\"EEE\" style=\"left:10px;top:220px;border:0;padding:0\"><input value=\"漢字\" style=\"left:200px;top:10px;padding:0;border:0\"><input value=\"سلام\" style=\"left:200px;top:80px;padding:0;border:0\"><input placeholder=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:150px;border:0;padding:0;height:40px\"><input type=\"submit\" value=\"EEE\" style=\"left:200px;top:220px;font-family:monospace\"></body></html>"
val FLOW: text = "<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><style>*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif;background:#fff;color:#fff}}label{{display:block;margin:8px 0}}input{{color:#000;background:#fff;padding:8px;border:1px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:5px}}</style></head><body><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\"></label><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\" style=\"font-family:monospace\"></label><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\" style=\"font-size:16px\"></label><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\" style=\"height:40px\"></label><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\" style=\"font-size:20px;font-family:monospace\"></label><label>Name <input value=\"EEE\" style=\"padding:0;border:0;height:30px;font-family:monospace\"></label></body></html>"

fn _red(px: u32) -> i32:
    ((px >> 16u32) & 0xFFu32) as i32

# "a..b " runs of rows holding ink (red < 128) in columns x0..x1, rows y0..y1.
fn _ink_rows(px: [u32], k: i32, x0: i32, x1: i32, y0: i32, y1: i32) -> text:
    val w = CSS_W * k
    if px.len() != (w * CSS_H * k) as i64:
        return "bad frame"
    var out = ""
    var start = -1
    var y = y0
    while y <= y1 + 1:
        var ink = false
        if y <= y1:
            var x = x0
            while x <= x1 and not ink:
                if _red(px[y * w + x]) < 128:
                    ink = true
                x = x + 1
        if ink and start < 0:
            start = y
        elif not ink and start >= 0:
            out = out + "{start}..{y - 1} "
            start = -1
        y = y + 1
    out

# The UA-font inputs of the ABS page at device scale k: left column
# (catalog-styled, monospace, default up to above its bottom border), then
# right column (no padding/border, height:40px, height:41px).
fn _abs_rows(k: i32) -> text:
    val px = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(ABS, CSS_W, CSS_H, k, "cpu_simd")
    (_ink_rows(px, k, 12 * k, 80 * k, 8 * k, 146 * k) + _ink_rows(px, k, 12 * k, 80 * k, 218 * k, 237 * k) + "| " +
        _ink_rows(px, k, 200 * k, 270 * k, 8 * k, 216 * k))

# Last ink row of columns x0..x1 in rows y0..y1 (device px), -1 for none.
fn _last_ink_row(px: [u32], k: i32, x0: i32, x1: i32, y0: i32, y1: i32) -> i32:
    val w = CSS_W * k
    if px.len() != (w * CSS_H * k) as i64:
        return -2
    var y = y1
    while y >= y0:
        var x = x0
        while x <= x1:
            if _red(px[y * w + x]) < 128:
                return y
            x = x + 1
        y = y - 1
    -1

describe "A text input value sits on Chrome's device line at device scale k (Chrome 159)":
    it "AC-1: at 4x the monospace and height:40px values are on rows 331 and 381":
        expect(_abs_rows(4)).to_equal("87..123 331..369 880..887 903..939 | 51..87 381..417 663..699 ")
    it "AC-2: at 4x in-flow inputs on label lines have value rows 79..115 244..282":
        val px = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(FLOW, CSS_W, CSS_H, 4, "cpu_simd")
        expect(_ink_rows(px, 4, 160, 800, 0, 350)).to_equal("79..115 244..282 ")
    it "AC-3: at 3x the values are on Chrome's rows (the monospace one by its last row, 275)":
        val px = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(ABS, CSS_W, CSS_H, 3, "cpu_simd")
        val sans = (_ink_rows(px, 3, 36, 240, 24, 228) + _ink_rows(px, 3, 36, 240, 654, 711) + "| " +
            _ink_rows(px, 3, 600, 810, 24, 648))
        expect(sans + "| {_last_ink_row(px, 3, 36, 240, 234, 438)}").to_equal("64..91 660..665 676..703 | 37..64 285..312 496..523 | 275")
    it "AC-4: at 2x the values are on Chrome's rows":
        expect(_abs_rows(2)).to_equal("44..61 164..183 440..443 452..469 | 26..43 191..208 332..349 ")
    it "AC-5: at 1x the rows stay where Chrome has them":
        val px = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(ABS, CSS_W, CSS_H, 1, "cpu_simd")
        expect(_ink_rows(px, 1, 12, 80, 8, 237) + "| " + _ink_rows(px, 1, 200, 270, 8, 290)).to_equal("22..30 82..91 152..163 220..221 226..234 | 13..21 96..104 166..174 225..238 ")
    it "AC-6: button-type values and placeholders are on Chrome's rows at 4x and 3x":
        val p4 = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(CTL, CSS_W, CSS_H, 4, "cpu_simd")
        val got4 = (_ink_rows(p4, 4, 72, 176, 56, 108) + _ink_rows(p4, 4, 40, 240, 312, 864) + _ink_rows(p4, 4, 832, 928, 896, 948) +
            "| {_last_ink_row(p4, 4, 40, 240, 872, 1160)} {_last_ink_row(p4, 4, 800, 1040, 592, 864)}")
        expect(got4).to_equal("63..99 331..367 661..697 903..941 | 927 697")
        val p3 = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(CTL, CSS_W, CSS_H, 3, "cpu_simd")
        val got3 = (_ink_rows(p3, 3, 54, 132, 42, 81) + _ink_rows(p3, 3, 30, 180, 234, 648) +
            "| {_last_ink_row(p3, 3, 30, 180, 654, 870)} {_last_ink_row(p3, 3, 600, 780, 444, 648)} {_last_ink_row(p3, 3, 624, 696, 672, 711)}")
        expect(got3).to_equal("46..73 247..274 495..522 | 694 522 704")
    it "AC-7: at 3x a fallback-font (Arabic) value keeps its face offset: rows 246..284":
        val px = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(CTL, CSS_W, CSS_H, 3, "cpu_simd")
        expect(_ink_rows(px, 3, 600, 780, 234, 438)).to_equal("246..284 ")
    it "AC-8: a 16px author-font input value is not moved: rows 460..492 at 3x, 307..328 at 2x":
        val p3 = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(ABS, CSS_W, CSS_H, 3, "cpu_simd")
        val p2 = simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(ABS, CSS_W, CSS_H, 2, "cpu_simd")
        expect(_ink_rows(p3, 3, 36, 240, 444, 648) + "| " + _ink_rows(p2, 2, 24, 160, 296, 432)).to_equal("460..492 | 307..328 ")
